&gt; As far as farming more efficiently, I'd like to point to the multiboxing community as a whole. 8 man boxers out herbing are absolutely more efficient than a single toon herbing, but yet I'm sure you still see obvious multiboxers undercutting by only 1c instead of by 30-50% of lowest buyout. Efficiency of obtaining an item is not the same as efficiency of making that item worth your time when selling it, depending on usefulness of said item. Hell I'd even go so far as to say efficiency of acquisition has little to do with our personal market values compared to the usefulness of the item.

Time/efficiency for attaining something is only 1/3rd of the equation.  Multiboxers won't dump their haul at bargain basement prices if they don't need to, but they do tend to aggressively undercut unless the demand is super high to move their stock, because otherwise it piles up, and that directly relates to availability and demand.

All three of those forces work together to determine the actual market value.  People can inflate that by trying to control the supply on the market with resets in the short term, but if overall demand is softer than supply, inevitably they'll be left with a few hundred stacks in their banks, bags, and mailboxes, and have to take a hit when they have to liquidate their stock.

